---
import NarrativeLayout from '../layouts/NarrativeLayout.astro';
import ThreeRetailerComparison from '../components/ThreeRetailerComparison.astro';
import ERDToggle from '../components/ERDToggle.astro';
import GTINHierarchy from '../components/GTINHierarchy.astro';
import EntityTable from '../components/EntityTable.astro';
import MarginMath from '../components/MarginMath.astro';

// Crosslink chips ("Built on: Dimension & Weight Integrity", "Built on:
// Product Data Health Audit", "Feeds: Item Setup Pre-flight") were removed
// 2026-07-06: the sibling pieces are not yet published, so the chips had dead
// href="#" targets. Restore the .crosslinks block (styles still below) with
// real URLs when those pieces ship — see HANDOFF.md.
---

<NarrativeLayout title="Product Master Data Model — Lailara LLC">

  <!-- Part 1: The Hook -->
  <section id="hook">
    <p class="orientation">Part 1 of 3 — The Problem</p>
    <h1>Walmart, Costco, and UNFI are not asking about the same product.</h1>
    <p>
      The same jar of Calabrian Chili Marinara enters three different item-setup
      forms at two different GTIN levels — Walmart keys on the each, Costco and
      UNFI key on the case. A flat product spreadsheet cannot represent this.
      Most specialty food brands discover that gap during their first retailer
      rejection.
    </p>
    <ThreeRetailerComparison />
  </section>

  <!-- Part 2: The Proof -->
  <section id="proof">
    <p class="orientation">Part 2 of 3 — The Model</p>
    <h2>Here is the model that prevents this.</h2>
    <p>
      One SKU — CHP-0009 — walked from brand through each, inner, case, and pallet.
      A GTIN assigned at every level that carries one. The attribute set each
      retailer demands, mapped to the entity that owns it.
    </p>

    <GTINHierarchy />

    <p>
      The case row states the problem plainly: the shipped dimensions are NULL.
      Costco and UNFI both require them. The model below assigns responsibility for filling them —
      one entity per obligation, one source of truth per field.
    </p>

    <ERDToggle />

    <h3>Each entity carries an obligation</h3>
    <p class="section-subtitle">
      What every node in the diagram is accountable for — and what breaks without it.
    </p>

    <EntityTable />
  </section>

  <!-- Part 3: The Evidence -->
  <section id="evidence">
    <p class="orientation">Part 3 of 3 — The Evidence</p>
    <h2>This isn't a whiteboard diagram — it's written as working DDL.</h2>
    <p>
      The model is documented in four Postgres tables that apply with
      <code>psql</code>. dbt model contracts and schema tests are specified and
      deferred until the Cinderhaven platform's Postgres instance is available.
      Published figures are checked by <code>check_canonical.py</code>, the
      drift guard in the Cinderhaven platform repo.
    </p>

    <div class="evidence-links">
      <div class="evidence-item">
        <span class="evidence-label">Data lineage</span>
        <span class="evidence-link evidence-link--text">dbt contracts — deployment in progress</span>
        <span class="evidence-note">dim_products and its satellite tables — column contracts, tests, lineage graph. Docs site publishes when the platform Postgres is live.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <span class="evidence-label">Proposed schema</span>
        <span class="evidence-link evidence-link--text">sql/ in this repository</span>
        <span class="evidence-note">Four DDL files defining the proposed extension to dim_products.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="evidence-item">
        <span class="evidence-label">Drift guard</span>
        <span class="evidence-link evidence-link--text"><code>check_canonical.py</code></span>
        <span class="evidence-note">Validates published figures against the Cinderhaven canonical dataset. Runs in the platform repo.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <MarginMath />


    <p class="evidence-footnote">
      Canonical figures as of <code>CINDERHAVEN_CANONICAL.md</code> last verified 2026-07-29
      against production. 50 SKUs · 6 retailers · 3 distributors + DTC · $32.3M retail scan
      revenue (CY2025).
      Data: Cinderhaven Provisions, a synthetic demonstration dataset (not a client).
    </p>
  </section>

</NarrativeLayout>

<style>
  /* Section dividers — London-85 rule at top of parts 2 and 3 */
  #proof,
  #evidence {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-gridline);
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  /* Part 3 — Evidence section */

  .evidence-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 1.5em 0;
    max-width: 660px;
  }

  .evidence-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    grid-template-rows: auto auto;
    gap: 2px 16px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .evidence-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .evidence-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    grid-row: 1;
    grid-column: 1;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .evidence-link {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-navy);
    grid-row: 1;
    grid-column: 2;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .evidence-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    color: var(--color-navy-hover);
  }

  .evidence-link--text {
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: default;
  }

  .evidence-note {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    grid-row: 2;
    grid-column: 2;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Cross-link chips */
  .crosslinks {
    margin: 2em 0 1.5em;
  }

  .crosslinks-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .crosslinks-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .chip {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: opacity 150ms ease-out;
  }

  .chip:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .chip--built-on {
    background: var(--color-info-bg);
    color: var(--color-info-text);
    border-color: var(--color-navy-light);
  }

  .chip--feeds {
    background: var(--color-pass-bg);
    color: var(--color-pass-text);
    border-color: var(--teal-7);
  }

  /* Footnote */
  .evidence-footnote {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: none;
    margin-top: 2em;
    padding-top: 1em;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-gridline);
  }

  /* Mobile */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .evidence-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .evidence-label {
      grid-row: 1;
      grid-column: 1;
    }

    .evidence-link,
    .evidence-link--text {
      grid-row: 2;
      grid-column: 1;
    }

    .evidence-note {
      grid-row: 3;
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
